<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<style>
    body {
        font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
        line-height: 1.6;
        color: #333;
        margin: 20px;
    }
    h1 {
        color: #1a5f7a;
        border-bottom: 2px solid #1a5f7a;
        padding-bottom: 8px;
    }
    h2 {
        color: #57c5b6;
        margin-top: 30px;
    }
    table {
        width: 100%;
        border-collapse: collapse;
        margin-bottom: 30px;
    }
    th, td {
        border: 1px solid #ddd;
        padding: 10px;
        text-align: left;
    }
    th {
        background-color: #f2f2f2;
        font-weight: bold;
        color: #1a5f7a;
    }
    tr:nth-child(even) {
        background-color: #fafafa;
    }
    .code {
        font-family: Consolas, monospace;
        background-color: #f8f8f8;
        padding: 2px 4px;
        border-radius: 3px;
        font-size: 0.9em;
    }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<h1>Schema Metadata Flow & Sample Data Walkthrough</h1>
<p>This document presents mock datasets for the <code>connectors</code> tables under two sample organizations to demonstrate how the database connections, schema structures, relationships, embeddings, and query logs link together.</p>

<h2>🏢 Organization Configurations</h2>
<ol>
    <li><strong>Organization 1:</strong> <code>qrioue_tech_llp</code>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>UUID:</strong> <span class="code">11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111</span></li>
            <li><strong>Database:</strong> PostgreSQL containing an ecommerce schema (<code>orders</code> &amp; <code>users</code> tables).</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Organization 2:</strong> <code>elite_evince_tech</code>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>UUID:</strong> <span class="code">22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222</span></li>
            <li><strong>Database:</strong> MySQL containing an HR schema (<code>employees</code> &amp; <code>departments</code> tables).</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ol>

<h2>🗄️ Table 1: connectors.database_connections</h2>
<p>Stores the metadata connection details to the external database.</p>
<table>
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Column</th>
            <th>Row 1 (qrioue_tech_llp)</th>
            <th>Row 2 (elite_evince_tech)</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>id</strong> (UUID)</td>
            <td><span class="code">55555555-5555-5555-5555-555555555555</span></td>
            <td><span class="code">66666666-6666-6666-6666-666666666666</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>organization_id</strong></td>
            <td><span class="code">11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111</span></td>
            <td><span class="code">22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>name</strong></td>
            <td>qrioue_ecommerce_db</td>
            <td>elite_hr_db</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>database_type</strong></td>
            <td>postgresql</td>
            <td>mysql</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>host</strong></td>
            <td>pg-host.qrioue.local</td>
            <td>mysql-host.elite.local</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>port</strong></td>
            <td>5432</td>
            <td>3306</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>database_name</strong></td>
            <td>prod_ecommerce</td>
            <td>company_hr</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>schema_name</strong></td>
            <td>public</td>
            <td>company_hr</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>username</strong></td>
            <td>qrioue_read</td>
            <td>elite_read</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>password</strong></td>
            <td>password_raw_or_encrypted</td>
            <td>password_raw_or_encrypted</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>is_active</strong></td>
            <td>true</td>
            <td>true</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>last_synced_at</strong></td>
            <td>2026-06-18 10:00:00</td>
            <td>2026-06-18 10:15:00</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>sync_status</strong></td>
            <td>synced</td>
            <td>synced</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>sync_error</strong></td>
            <td>null</td>
            <td>null</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

